OL,3,GNEWSA'We're still cold paying #300 a
OL,4,Amonth energy bills'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA pensioner says trying to keep warm
OL,7,Fand afford heating this winter will be
OL,8,F"horrific" amid rising energy costs.
OL,10,FPat Snell, from Redditch,
OL,11,FWorcestershire, said she and her
OL,12,Fhusband, John, who had a stroke, relied
OL,13,Fheavily on heating to keep him
OL,14,Fcomfortable last winter.
OL,16,F"Even on a fixed-price tariff, our
OL,17,Fenergy bills were #300 a month, and we
OL,18,Fwere still cold," she said.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
